WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.220
There are many times when you need to add
stitches to the edge of your knitting.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.420
A pattern may read "cast on 20
stitches on the right side".

3
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.780
Using a cast-on rag makes this process

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.260
easier by giving you scrap
knitting to hang weight.

5
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:20.020
Cast-on rag is reusable and it can also
be used is for starting your knitting

6
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:27.660
saving Scrap Yarn. To create a cast-on rag,
use a strong, tightly twisted yarn.

7
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.380
You'll be knitting a diagonal piece.

8
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.740
Start at the left edge of your needlebed
and cast on four to five stitches.

9
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.060
Knit a few rows and end
with your carriage on the right.

10
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.380
On the left side, decrease one stitch.

11
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.180
I'm using a two-pronged tool.

12
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.660
Use whatever is comfortable for you.

13
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.140
Put the empty needle out of work
on the right side.

14
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.300
Pull one needle into work.

15
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.180
Knit two rows.

16
00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.700
You'll notice that a loop is
formed over the new needle.

17
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.580
This is the key to the caston rag.

18
00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.410
Continue to decrease left and increase

19
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.240
right until the piece
is the desired length.

20
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.340
The knitting will travel across the bed

21
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:19.410
and you may need to take all the stitches
off and rehang them on the left side again

22
00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.340
to continue making the rag longer.
If you crochet.

23
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:29.180
Another quick way of making a reusable
cast on rag is with crochet.

24
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.620
Simply work a piece with smooth
yarn the width you need.

25
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:38.140
Double crochet, single crochet,
whatever works for your yarn.

26
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.740
Hang the edges of the crochet row

27
00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:48.180
on the needles, knit one row of ravel
cord and then use this to hang weight.

28
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.780
You can now either cast
on with the garment yarn over the ravel

29
00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:56.420
cord or just start knitting
for a provisional caston.

30
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.420
When you remove the ravel cord,

31
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:03.180
you'll have the crochet rag
to use over and over again.

32
00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:08.450
If I'm only casting on a few stitches
and I'm in a hurry, I'll confess that I've

33
00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.780
resorted to using a swatch
that's lying around.

34
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.260
I hang the edge of the swatch.

35
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.260
On the needles, hang some weights
and knit a row of ravel I cord.

36
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.060
I can then begin working right away.

37
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.940
With the garment yarn without having to.

38
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.450
Find my cast on rag.

39
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.860
If you have knitting on the machine
and you are adding stitches,

40
00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.940
use the cast-on rag. End with the carriage
and the yarn from the yarn feeder

41
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:39.220
on the right,
hang one loop on each needle as needed.

42
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:43.400
Hang weights also as needed.

43
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.720
Manually knit a row of ravel cord.

44
00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.980
Then, using the yarn from the yarn feeder,

45
00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:25.680
cast on the new needles using the method
of your choice.

46
00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:48.360
Knit across all the needles and continue
knitting as directed in your pattern.

47
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.780
When you finish knitting,

48
00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:12.820
remove the ravel cord
and set aside the cast-on and rag.

49
00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.640
And you'll see you have a very neat edge.

